{"q":"20","t":"Valid Parentheses","d":"Easy","p":false,"c":"<p>Given a string <code>s</code> containing just the characters <code>&#39;(&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;)&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;{&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;}&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;[&#39;</code> and <code>&#39;]&#39;</code>, determine if the input string is valid.</p>\n\n<p>An input string is valid if:</p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Open brackets must be closed by the same type of brackets.</li>\n\t<li>Open brackets must be closed in the correct order.</li>\n\t<li>Every close bracket has a corresponding open bracket of the same type.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">s = &quot;()&quot;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">true</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">s = &quot;()[]{}&quot;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">true</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">s = &quot;(]&quot;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">false</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 4:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">s = &quot;([])&quot;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">true</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 5:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">s = &quot;([)]&quot;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">false</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= s.length &lt;= 10<sup>4</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>s</code> consists of parentheses only <code>&#39;()[]{}&#39;</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n","h":["Use a stack of characters.","When you encounter an opening bracket, push it to the top of the stack.","When you encounter a closing bracket, check if the top of the stack was the opening for it. If yes, pop it from the stack. Otherwise, return false."],"m":"{ \r\n  \"name\": \"isValid\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    { \r\n      \"name\": \"s\",\r\n      \"type\": \"string\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"boolean\"\r\n  }\r\n}","g":[{"name":"String","slug":"string"},{"name":"Stack","slug":"stack"},{"name":"Bracket Sequences","slug":"bracket-sequences"}],"s":[{"t":"Generate Parentheses","s":"generate-parentheses","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Longest Valid Parentheses","s":"longest-valid-parentheses","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"Remove Invalid Parentheses","s":"remove-invalid-parentheses","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"Check If Word Is Valid After Substitutions","s":"check-if-word-is-valid-after-substitutions","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Check if a Parentheses String Can Be Valid","s":"check-if-a-parentheses-string-can-be-valid","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Move Pieces to Obtain a String","s":"move-pieces-to-obtain-a-string","d":"Medium","p":false}],"co":[["Google","google"],["Meta","facebook"],["Amazon","amazon"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["BlackRock","blackrock"],["Microsoft","microsoft"],["LinkedIn","linkedin"],["Intuit","intuit"],["IBM","ibm"],["Tripadvisor","tripadvisor"],["tcs","tcs"],["Autodesk","autodesk"],["Virtu Financial","virtu"],["Oracle","oracle"],["Nvidia","nvidia"],["Apple","apple"],["Epic Systems","epic-systems"],["TikTok","tiktok"],["Infosys","infosys"],["Cognizant","cognizant"],["Tesla","tesla"],["ServiceNow","servicenow"],["Adobe","adobe"],["Two Sigma","two-sigma"],["Yandex","yandex"],["Qualcomm","qualcomm"],["Walmart Labs","walmart-labs"],["Zoho","zoho"],["Wells Fargo","wells-fargo"],["FreshWorks",